.TH MINIMAL-AIS-JSON 1
.SH NAME
minimal-ais-json \- write a JSON scoreboard from UDP AIS messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minimal-ais-json
.B \-l
.I address:port
.B \-o
.I file.json
[
.B \-a
.I duration
]
[
.B \-v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minimal-ais-json
listens for UDP NMEA AIS sentences and writes a JSON file containing the latest
known data by MMSI.
.PP
The program processes AIS message types 1, 2, 3, 4, 18, 21, and 24. It tracks
sender type, name, location, heading, speed, MMSI, update time, and last-seen
time. Output is sorted by MMSI.
.PP
The JSON file is rewritten when a processed sentence changes the scoreboard and
at least once a minute while the program is running. Entries older than the
maximum age are dropped before writing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-l " address:port"
UDP address and port to listen on. IPv6 addresses must be written as
.IR [address]:port .
.TP
.BI \-o " file.json"
JSON output file. The program writes a temporary file next to this path and then
renames it into place.
.TP
.BI \-a " duration"
Drop entries not seen within this interval. The default is
.BR 12h .
Durations may be bare seconds or use
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
.BR h ,
or
.BR d .
.TP
.B \-v
Print each valid AIS sentence before processing it.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
minimal-ais-json -l 0.0.0.0:10110 -o /run/minimal-ais/current.json -a 12h
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minimal-ais-serial (1)
